From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:02:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] package/ffmpeg: bump to version 7.1.2

At the end of the input, the ffmpeg 6.1 command line tool takes every
frame the decoder still returns into its filter graph before it runs the
graph. With a V4L2 mem2mem decoder those frames hold CAPTURE buffers, so
a decoder that needs a CAPTURE buffer back to finish draining waits
forever. On the Qualcomm venus decoder (QCM2290), a 60-frame 1280x720
H.264 stream hangs after V4L2_DEC_CMD_STOP with 58 frames decoded and 18
of the 20 CAPTURE buffers held by ffmpeg. ffmpeg 7.0 runs filtering in
its own thread, which keeps returning the buffers while the decoder
drains.

Use the release tarball, whose signature can be checked. Drop
--disable-crystalhd: 7.0 removed the decoder and configure rejects the
option. Rebase 0001 and 0003; drop 0005, 0006 and 0007, which 7.1.2
already contains.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
